const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"手册章节说明如何把金融中介和信贷政策经由资产负债表及信贷市场机制纳入商业周期分析。 阅读时应将其放回原始样本、时点和制度环境中理解，不能把问题本身当作跨市场结论。",en:"The handbook chapter explains how financial intermediaries and credit policy can be incorporated into business-cycle analysis through balance-sheet and credit-market mechanisms. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-444-53238-1.00011-9",label:{zh:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它是理论与综述框架而不是单一实证估计量；中介约束、契约结构、政策规则和均衡假设定义每个机制。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中任一选择，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It is a theoretical and survey-oriented framework rather than a single empirical estimator, so intermediary constraints, contract structure, policy rule, and equilibrium assumptions define each mechanism. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-444-53238-1.00011-9",label:{zh:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"实证应用需要带日期的银行和中介资产负债表、借贷与融资条款、信用利差、政策行动、借款人特征、宏观总量、监管制度及概念到观测值的映射。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选必须与原研究分开记录，不能因变量同名或使用最新修订值便视为可比。",en:"An empirical application needs dated bank and intermediary balance sheets, lending and funding terms, credit spreads, policy actions, borrower characteristics, macro aggregates, regulatory regimes, and a stated mapping from concepts to observables. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-444-53238-1.00011-9",label:{zh:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"章节组织中介条件和政策可能影响宏观波动的传导渠道，并不识别某家银行风险、实时信贷冲击或具体政策处方。 它只支持来源描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The chapter organizes channels through which intermediary conditions and policy can matter for macro fluctuations; it does not identify a particular bank's risk, a live credit shock, or a policy prescription. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-444-53238-1.00011-9",label:{zh:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"声明模型中的中介摩擦；区分存量和流量；保留监管与会计制度；对齐政策公告和实施日期；将模型假设与观测相关性分开。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"State the modeled intermediary friction; distinguish stock from flow measures; preserve regulatory and accounting regimes; align policy announcements and implementation dates; and keep model assumptions separate from observed correlations. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-444-53238-1.00011-9",label:{zh:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record。金融中介框架不是当前因果通道的证据、信贷建议或对机构监管分析的替代。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record. A framework for financial intermediation is not evidence of a current causal channel, a credit recommendation, or a substitute for institution-specific supervisory analysis. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-444-53238-1.00011-9",label:{zh:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Handbook of Monetary Economics · DOI record · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Financial Intermediation and Credit Policy in Business Cycle Analysis”公开说明的研究对象、设计与适用边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。金融中介框架不是当前因果通道的证据、信贷建议或对机构监管分析的替代。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Financial Intermediation and Credit Policy in Business Cycle Analysis”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
